R2 -- Burnside A000568 even-cycle vanishing = the involution on sigma-edge-orbits
==================================================================================
        sigma cycle type  has even cycle   Fix(sigma)
  n=4       [1, 1, 1, 1]           False           64
  n=4          [1, 1, 2]            True            0
  n=4             [1, 3]           False            4
  n=4             [2, 2]            True            0
  n=4                [4]            True            0
  n=5    [1, 1, 1, 1, 1]           False         1024
  n=5       [1, 1, 1, 2]            True            0
  n=5          [1, 1, 3]           False           16
  n=5          [1, 2, 2]            True            0
  n=5             [1, 4]            True            0
  n=5             [2, 3]            True            0
  n=5                [5]           False            4
  n=6 [1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1]           False        32768
  n=6    [1, 1, 1, 1, 2]            True            0
  n=6       [1, 1, 1, 3]           False          128
  n=6       [1, 1, 2, 2]            True            0
  n=6          [1, 1, 4]            True            0
  n=6          [1, 2, 3]            True            0
  n=6             [1, 5]           False            8
  n=6          [2, 2, 2]            True            0
  n=6             [2, 4]            True            0
  n=6             [3, 3]           False           32
  n=6                [6]            True            0
  => Fix=0 IFF sigma has an even cycle (even => vanish, all-odd => survive): the
     A000568 Burnside dichotomy is the sign/parity involution on edge-orbits.

==================================================================================
R3 -- moment discriminant collapse: interference of balanced tuples = tournament sum
==================================================================================
  The Vandermonde of the CHARGE points c_1<...<c_k controls whether distinct balanced
  character-tuples cancel.  It is the SAME signed tournament sum; it is NONZERO iff the
  charges are DISTINCT (transitive/one-sided survivor).  Single-character (THM-1840) has
  ONE atom => one surviving term => never cancels (clean nullcone base case).
    charges (2, 3): Vandermonde(discriminant seed) = 1  (nonzero <=> distinct)
    charges (1, 4): Vandermonde(discriminant seed) = 3  (nonzero <=> distinct)
    charges (2, 3, 5): Vandermonde(discriminant seed) = 6  (nonzero <=> distinct)
    charges (1, 2, 3, 4): Vandermonde(discriminant seed) = 12  (nonzero <=> distinct)
  => 'transitive survives' on the moment side = 'distinct charges / one-sided stratum
     is the deep nullcone point' (THM-1815); interference vanishes exactly off it.

==================================================================================
PUNCHLINE -- where the engine STOPS: LRC
==================================================================================
  The involution needs CLEAN +/-1 signs (charges/factorials give (-1)^back-arcs). The LRC
  covering sum sum_{k.v=0} prod sinc(k_j delta) has TRANSCENDENTAL sinc weights, not signs
  -- so no 3-cycle sign-reversing involution is available, and the covering does NOT
  collapse to a transitive core.  That missing involution IS the S157 measure barrier
  (factorial monotone/clean vs sinc oscillating) restated combinatorially.
